From 020582149f020ef07e8d6dff111ed7ece79cd317 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:32:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Applications privacy, Network Manager and App
 Security model

Pure Java (no android.* imports) model for the SableOS Applications
work ported from the GrapheneOS-era UI5A/UI5B/R9 Settings patches:

* PrivacyEvaluator, AppPrivacy, PrivacyRow: the sensitive-access
  summary under an app name. Same groups, order, density (three labels
  then +N, special access as a warning marker) and truthfulness rule
  as Sable Start's All Apps row (DESIGN-KF-D): a group needs an
  effective grant in the app's own user, an ignored/errored App-op
  cancels it, an unreadable op is UNKNOWN and never shown as access.
* NetworkAccessPolicy, NetworkAppRows: Network Manager over the
  per-UID restriction bits LineageOS already enforces. The one switch
  adds or removes only the all-networks bit; transport bits set in
  App info are reported, never hidden or cleared. Shared-UID packages
  share one row. Blocking a messaging app asks first.
* ComponentExposure, NativeCodeScan, AppSecurityFacts, Evidence: the
  read-only App Security & Privacy page (component exposure, bounded
  APK native-code inspection that is UNKNOWN when nothing was read,
  install class, installer chain, signer digest).

SettingsSableAppsModelTests runs them on the host JVM.
